\begin{customfact}{1} Let $\cX$ be a non-hyperelliptic compact Riemann surface of genus $g=3$. If the  automorphism group of $\cX$ acts transitively on the Weierstrass points then $\cX \in \mathscr{K}_3.$
\end{customfact}

